Z||000002||fierohoho||09-03-2001||03:34 AM||||Blackdragon, a heads up display allows you to see your speed, rpm's, oil pressure and any thing eles you want by looking straight ahead as the image (which is usually red LED) is reflected on the windshield in front of the driver. That way you keep your eyes on the road and off the instruments.<P>Hope that helps. <P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pennockpic.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||09-03-2001||07:15 AM||||It seems to me that a HUD display would be distracting on a long trip. I,ve never used one. Can anyone speak from experience driving with one ?||||reg||5
Z||000004||formula2||09-03-2001||09:02 AM||||I have heads up display in my 97 Grand-Prix.<BR>At first, it is distracting, but after a few weeks, you get use to it..<BR>I wish now that all cars have that feature.||||reg||14
